<title>USA: Clinton proposes limited haying, grazing on CRP.</title>
<headline>Clinton proposes limited haying, grazing on CRP.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers would be allowed to harvest hay or graze livestock on the Conservation Reserve on a limited basis under the fiscal 1998 budget proposed by President Clinton.</p>
<p>Budget documents also said the administration had a goal of enrolling 36.4 million acres in the reserve, the maximum allowed. New operating rules for the reserve are due soon.</p>
<p>Under the proposal, haying and grazing would be allowed once every three years and the rental payment that year would be cut in half. It would save the government $25 million.</p>
<p>Conservation Reserve Program pays farmers to retire land for 10 years.</p>
</text>
